# Python float-fix static gate — review report

Scope: full uncommitted diff vs base 69e58662 (15 files, +290/−83) plus untracked `test/yang/python/antlr/float_address_test.cljc`, checked against the converged float-address ruling (yang.antlr.md §8.5 float paragraph, the diff's own lines 1249–1271) and the UCF/cbor doc deltas. Read-only: no files touched; lints ran cache-free (`clj-kondo --cache false`, `cljstyle check`).

## Ruling fidelity (verified, not findings)

Every concrete clause of the ruling is realized: lowering builds `{:py/float (cbor/float64 x)}` (`lower.cljc:282`); `py/float` wraps through `data/float64` and `py/num` unwraps through `data/float-value` (`prelude.cljc:99,112`); every prelude float constant is now a `data/float-value` operand and no integral float literal survives (`prelude.cljc:859,877-879,906,941-944,953-954,966,984-986,1047-1049`), enforced per-load by `float-literal-defects` (`float_address_test.cljc:172-210`); dict/set keys normalize via `data/numeric-key` with the ±(2^53−1) rule (`data.cljc:452-464`, call site `prelude.cljc:1197`); the carrier is admitted at all three scalar gates (`vm.cljc:1002,1021`, `engine.cljc:640`). No unary one-arg `-` on floats was introduced (all changed arithmetic is two-arg or `(* -1.0 x)`-shaped); all new reader conditionals keep `:cljd` first per the `dao.jing.cbor` convention; `render.cljc`/`lower.cljc` gaining `yin.vm.data`/`dao.jing.cbor` follows existing yang→yin/dao edges (`yang/safepoint.cljc`, `yang/tails.cljc`) and creates no cycle (cbor requires no yin.*). `data/numeric-key` is cleanly isolated for the C3-S2 rebase: exactly four deletion sites (`data.cljc:452-464`, `data.cljc:504`, `prelude.cljc:89`, `prelude.cljc:1197`) plus the two test entries; no callers outside the float path. Kondo: 0 errors; only pre-existing warnings outside the diff hunks, plus one new info (below).

## Findings

**P2 | docs/design/yang.antlr.md:1266-1268 | The diff adds a behavior the 8.5.5 ruling paragraph does not record: `vm.cljc:374-420` (`carrier-refusing`, `refuse-carrier`) makes generic-yin `+ - * / < > <= >=` throw `{:yin.k/status :yin.k/non-portable, :yin.k/kind :float64-carrier, :yin.k/name op}` on JS, tested by `float_address_test.cljc:316-335`. The ruling paragraph records only admission ("The VM admits the carrier as a scalar at `plain-data?`, `machine-data?` and the lift and pin `scalar?` gate") and the UCF delta (yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:741-744) likewise records only admission; the arithmetic refusal — JS-only, deliberately asymmetric, and load-bearing (it is what stops `+` from coercing a carrier through its text) — is undocumented in the master design docs a future rebase reconciles against. | Add one sentence to the float paragraph (e.g. "Generic yin has no float seam: on JavaScript the standard arithmetic and ordering primitives refuse the carrier as `:yin.k/non-portable`; only a profile with an explicit `data/float-value` bridge computes on it") and, if desired, a clause in the UCF scalar-arm paragraph.

**P2 | test/yang/python/antlr/float_address_test.cljc:145-165 | NaN is the one stated float behavior with no coverage. ±0.0 (segment keys :155-160, repr :161-162, dict key :338-360), infinities (repr via `py/float-mod`/`float-divmod` cases, prelude_parity_test.cljc:279-301) and integer-valued floats (:139-157) are pinned, but nothing asserts the NaN path of the new seam on any host: `(render/float-repr (cbor/float64 ##NaN))` → `"nan"` (render.cljc:36-38), the one-quiet-NaN byte golden `(b64 (cbor/float64 ##NaN))` (the `"000000000000f87f"` claim, debruijn.cljc:875, debruijn_code.cljc:243), or a float program printing NaN. The NaN-key pin is explicitly deferred to C3-S2 (data.cljc:456-459) — that deferral is fine; NaN repr/bytes are current behavior and currently unexercised on the Node/CLJD lanes. `py/finite?`'s rewritten `##Inf` bridge (prelude.cljc:859) is likewise called by nothing. | Add to `canonical-bytes-test`: the NaN b64 golden, `(is (= "nan" (render/float-repr (cbor/decode …))))`, and `(is (not= (jing/segment-key (cbor/float64 ##NaN)) (jing/segment-key (cbor/float64 1))))`; one parity form `(py/eq (py/float-mod 0.0 ##Inf) {:py/float 0.0})`-style NaN producer with expected `"nan"` covers arithmetic.

**P3 | src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/render.cljc:36 | New kondo info introduced by this diff: "Redundant double coercion: expression already has type double" — `(data/float-value f)` (line 33) is now `:clj`-inferred as a double, so `(Double/isNaN (double x))` coerces twice. | Drop the inner coercion: `(Double/isNaN x)`. (Same one-liner applies to the mirrored copies at debruijn.cljc:879 and debruijn_code.cljc:247 if those are ever retyped the same way; they are pre-existing and kondo-clean today.)

**P3 | src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:112-113,906,986 | 8 added source lines exceed 80 columns: prelude.cljc 112 (88), 113 (89), 906 (98), 986 (90); debruijn.cljc:885 (84, pure reindent); debruijn_code.cljc:250 (84, pure reindent); test prelude_parity_test.cljc:177,194,195,299; data_test.cljc:311,326; and 12 in the untracked float_address_test.cljc (68, 75, 147, 162, 216, 218, 236, 238, 240, 244, 333, 360). Evidence: `awk 'length>80'` over the added-line set. The repo has no enforced width rule (`.cljstyle` configures none; prelude.cljc alone already carries 100+ over-length lines), so this is continuity, not regression — most offenders are unbreakable golden strings (base64/segment-key constants). | Wrap the four prelude expression lines and the six test-harness lines (`is`/`reduce` bodies); leave the golden-string lines or re-break the base64 literals.

**P3 | src/cljc/yin/vm/data.cljc:462 | `numeric-key` has no argument guard of its own; a non-number reaches `float-value` and is refused there, so `(call 'numeric-key "2")` reports `'float-value` as the refusing op instead of `'numeric-key` (contrast `float-value`'s own explicit guard at :430-432, which data_test.cljc:315 pins). Behavior is correct (it refuses), the op name in the refusal is just indirect, and C3-S2 deletes the function anyway. | Either accept as-is (documented interim), or add `(when-not (or (data-number? x) (cbor/float64? x)) (wrong-type! 'numeric-key 0 :number))` mirroring `float-value`.

## Not repeated from the brief, checked and clean

`=`/`==`/`!=` deliberately outside `carrier-refusing` matches its docstring contract (`vm.cljc:374-380` vs registry `vm.cljc:419-421`); the hand-rolled ex-info in `refuse-carrier` reuses engine's established `:yin.k/status`/`:yin.k/kind`/`:yin.k/name` vocabulary (`engine.cljc:627-630`); `values/kind-of` (:193-195) only feeds refusal metadata; every registry consumer goes through `primitive-function`, and the one raw-host-`+` test site was fixed (`completion_test.cljc:384-387`); the quoted prelude holds `data/*` only as symbols, so `prelude.cljc` needs no host require; `host-names` additions keep `e2e_test.clj:196` consistent; cljstyle check passes clean on all changed files; no tabs, no trailing whitespace, `:eof-newline` satisfied.

Prior reports in `collab/*floatfix*` were not consulted. Test suites were not run, per the gate's terms; the JVM/Node/CLJD lanes remain the orchestrator's to report.
